    "created_at": "2026-03-23T20:55:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-23T20:55:09Z",
    "body": "> What if opening an auto popover didn't close an ancestor hint popover?\n\nThat's a fairly large \"what if\", since it requires re-thinking the entire two stack model.\n\nI guess I don't understand the use case for \"hint that opens an auto\". The whole point/definition of a \"hint\" is that it is an even more ephemeral version of `popover=auto`, which is **subordinate** to `popover=auto`. It therefore doesn't support this inverted subordination (`auto` inside `hint`).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
