    "created_at": "2026-03-23T21:29:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-23T21:30:09Z",
    "body": "> But this is intentionally _not_ something the developer is supposed to be doing: nesting an `auto` inside a `hint` isn't a supported use case.\n\nBut that's my point, it isn't very intentional. The only place I found a reference to it being wrong is in the name of a wpt test.\n\nIt should either work in some non-broken way, or it should 'throw' because it's an invalid state.\n\nI'm not sure which would be best. But it doesn't seem like there's a particularly strong two stack model, since hint popovers can easily and confusingly end up in the auto stack https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12304",
