    "created_at": "2026-03-24T00:03:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-24T00:03:44Z",
    "body": "> But that's my point, it isn't very intentional. The only place I found a reference to it being wrong is in the name of a wpt test.\n\nI think you're likely pointing out (accurately) a documentation problem? But the spec and behavior were extensively discussed. Please read the hundreds of comments (each) on the issue and PR:\n\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9776\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9778\n\nI started with a much simpler model, where there was only a single hint, and not a full stack. But others (rightly, I think) pointed out use cases where you'd want stacks, and where you'd want a hint to reside in the auto stack, etc. Those were distilled down (after the discussions above converged on a direction for the spec) into the explainer section here: https://open-ui.org/components/popover-hint.research.explainer/#popover-stacks. Perhaps that helps a little?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
