    "created_at": "2026-03-26T16:05:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-26T16:05:06Z",
    "body": "> > That's a fairly large \"what if\", since it requires re-thinking the entire two stack model.\n> \n> The thing is there's not actually two stacks in the spec, there's the top layer set and functions that filter that down. I think we could just change the logic around which items from the top layer we care about (or make an actual seperate stacks).\n\nThat's effectively the same thing though. We originally had the spec PR with two actual stacks (which is how Chromium also implements it) but @annevk prefered the pseudo stack approach where the top layer is filtered (in the [auto](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#auto-popover-list) and [hint](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#showing-hint-popover-list) algorithms). But that's exactly equivalent to having two stacks.",
